Advantages and Disadvantages of this, hence what came next
==========================================================

Advantages
----------
1. Protects DHCP address pools.
2. Prevents DHCP Denial of Service attacks.
3. Blocks excessive DHCP requests.
4. Maintains availability for legitimate users.
5. Easy to implement.
6. Works with DHCP Snooping.
7. Improves network stability.

Disadvantages
-------------
1. Incorrect rate limits may affect genuine users.
2. Different networks require different thresholds.
3. Additional monitoring may be required.
4. Only protects DHCP-related attacks.
5. Does not validate ARP traffic.

Hence what came next
--------------------
After protecting DHCP services, attackers shifted their focus to ARP.

An attacker could send fake ARP messages claiming:

"I am the Default Gateway"

Traffic would then flow through the attacker's system.

This attack is called:

ARP Spoofing

To stop this attack, Cisco introduced:

Dynamic ARP Inspection (DAI)

which validates ARP packets using the DHCP Snooping Binding Table.

One-Shot Configuration
======================

Enable DHCP Snooping

Switch(config)# ip dhcp snooping

Switch(config)# ip dhcp snooping vlan 10,20,30


Configure Trusted Port
(DHCP Server/Uplink Port)

Switch(config)# interface g0/1
Switch(config-if)# ip dhcp snooping trust


Configure DHCP Rate Limiting on User Ports

Switch(config)# interface range fa0/1-24
Switch(config-if-range)# ip dhcp snooping limit rate 15


(Optional) Enable Auto Recovery

Switch(config)# errdisable recovery cause dhcp-rate-limit
Switch(config)# errdisable recovery interval 300

Verification
============

show ip dhcp snooping

show ip dhcp snooping statistics

show ip dhcp snooping binding

show errdisable recovery

